+# fullsend auto-merge (experimental)
+
+`fullsend auto-merge config [--config-dir .fullsend]` prints validated effective
+settings as JSON. It reads the overlay, base and defaults through the normal
+configuration loader. It makes no forge calls and never requests a merge.
+
+See [configuration reference](../reference/config-reference.md#experimental-auto-merge-configuration).
diff --git a/docs/guides/getting-started/repo-management.md b/docs/guides/getting-started/repo-management.md
index 26d418da..9dfcaf3a 100644
--- a/docs/guides/getting-started/repo-management.md
+++ b/docs/guides/getting-started/repo-management.md
@@ -1061,3 +1061,25 @@ commands.
 - [Operations](operations.md) — Day-2 per-repo administration and standalone commands
 - [CLI Reference: fullsend repos](../../cli/repos.md) — Full flag and subcommand reference
 - [Mint administration](../infrastructure/mint-administration.md) — Token mint deployment and management
+
+### Experimental auto-merge settings
+
+The local auto-merge experiment uses the same typed block at
+`defaults.config.auto_merge`, a forge's `config.auto_merge`, or a repository's
+`config.auto_merge`. For example:
+
+```yaml
+version: 1
+github:
+  repos:
+    - name: example/project
+      config:
+        auto_merge:
+          mode: shadow
+          policy: fullsend-default
+          controls: [OSPS-QA-03.01]
+```
+
+The selected integration must separately be installed. See the
+[experimental configuration reference](../../reference/config-reference.md#experimental-auto-merge-configuration)
+for modes, supported controls, inheritance and safety semantics.
