index 0bf1e5fd..4cfbd7bd 100644
--- a/docs/reference/config-reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference/config-reference.md
@@ -555,3 +555,35 @@ code defaults. For complete merge rules, see
   agents via config and harness
 - [`fullsend agent`](../cli/agent.md) — CLI commands for managing registered
   agents
+
+## Experimental auto-merge configuration
+
+The local experimental build accepts this block in `.fullsend/config.yaml`
+and in any managed `config:` block in `repos.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+auto_merge:
+  mode: shadow
+  policy: fullsend-default
+  controls:
+    - OSPS-QA-03.01
+```
+
+`mode` is `off` (default), `shadow` (evaluate without allowing a merge request),
+or `enforce`. `policy` currently accepts only `fullsend-default` (default).
+`controls` selects optional upstream requirements; this experiment supports only
+`OSPS-QA-03.01`. Omitted fields inherit individually; `mode: off` overrides an
+inherited enable, and `controls: []` clears inherited optional controls.
+Unknown modes, policies, controls and nested keys are rejected.
+
+Use `fullsend auto-merge config --config-dir .fullsend` to print effective JSON.
+A kill switch forces the resolved mode to off. Changing a preset cannot
+implicitly enable enforced merging or remove an existing control through
+managed convergence; declare a relaxation explicitly in the managed overlay.
+
+These settings do not install a writer, grant permissions or renew an owner
+grant. The auto-merge lab supplies the GitHub evidence adapter and existing
+protected-queue writer. They consume trusted target-branch configuration using
+the vendored binary. Other repositories need that integration before these
+settings have operational effect. This is an experimental schema, not a
+released Fullsend auto-merge feature.
